      "title": "HSY Q3 Earnings Top Estimates on Cost Relief and Pricing Gains",
      "summary": "The Hershey Company reported strong Q3 2026 earnings of $2.64 per share, up 103.1% year-over-year, driven by strategic pricing actions, tariff refunds, and lower commodity costs. However, the company faced volume declines due to pricing elasticity and cautious consumer spending. Net sales rose 3% to $3.28 billion, with adjusted gross margins expanding significantly. Management raised its 2026 earnings outlook to 36-38.5% growth but acknowledged ongoing challenges in convenience stores and salty snacks supply constraints.",
